+"""Durations as typed in the booking form."""
+
+import re
+
+# "1h30m", "1h 30m", "1h30", "1h", "45m". Minutes alone need the "m"; "30" on its own is not a duration.
+_MINUTES_ONLY = re.compile(r"^([0-9]+)m$")
+_HOURS = re.compile(r"^([0-9]+)h(?:\s*([0-9]+)m?)?$")
+
+
+def parse_duration(text):
+    """Turn a duration such as '45m', '1h', '1h30' or '1h 30m' into a number of minutes."""
+    cleaned = str(text).strip()
+    match = _MINUTES_ONLY.match(cleaned)
+    if match is not None:
+        minutes = int(match.group(1))
+    else:
+        match = _HOURS.match(cleaned)
+        if match is None:
+            raise ValueError(f"not a duration: {text!r}")
+        hours, rest = match.group(1), match.group(2)
+        minutes = int(hours) * 60 + (int(rest) if rest is not None else 0)
+        if rest is not None and int(rest) >= 60:
+            raise ValueError(f"minutes must be under 60 after hours: {text!r}")
+    if minutes == 0:
+        raise ValueError(f"duration must be more than zero: {text!r}")
+    return minutes
diff --git a/tests/test_intervals.py b/tests/test_intervals.py
